  "emoji": "🎓",
  "summary": "The last day of the course: say what you will do next with سَـ and أَنْ + a verb, give and take advice on how to keep learning, and say thank you and goodbye at a graduation party.",
  "intro": "Ninety days ago you learned your first letter; today is the حَفْلَةُ التَّخَرُّج, the graduation party. Everyone gets a شَهَادَة (certificate) and says what comes next, so today brings back two rules you know well. For plans, put سَـ in front of a present verb: سَأُسَافِرُ (I will travel), سَأَسْتَمِرُّ (I will keep on). For wishes and goals, use أَنْ + a present verb ending in -a: أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَتَعَلَّمَ (I want to learn), هَدَفِي أَنْ أَقْرَأَ (my goal is to read). Mr Karim's advice uses the imperative: اِقْرَؤُوا يَوْمِيًّا (read daily). And to thank someone warmly, say نَحْنُ مُمْتَنُّونَ لَكَ (we are grateful to you).",
  "objectives": [
    "Talk about your plans for the future with سَـ and سَوْفَ",
    "Say what you want to do and what your goal is with أَنْ + a verb in -a",
    "Give advice on how to keep learning: read daily, listen to the news, find a conversation partner",
    "Thank a teacher and say goodbye with the words for grateful, farewell and remember"
  ],
