    "culture": "Arabic has warm phrases for every goodbye. At a graduation people say مَبْرُوك (congratulations) and the reply is اللّٰه يُبَارِكُ فِيكَ (God bless you). When friends part, they say إِلَى اللِّقَاء (until we meet again) and, about any plan for the future, إِنْ شَاءَ اللّٰه (God willing). Learners who move on to a dialect find that standard Arabic, الْفُصْحَى, is the best base: the news, books and formal speech are in it everywhere.",
